.\n\n## Dataset 1: GSM8K (\"'`gsm8k`, config=`main`)\n\n### Overview\n- Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/gsm8k\n- Size: train 7,473 / test 1,319\n- Format: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- Task: Grade-school math reasoning with final-answer correctness\n- Splits: train, test\n- License: see dataset card on HuggingFace\n\n### Download Instructions\nUsing HuggingFace (recommended):\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"gsm8k\", \"main\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/gsm8k\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/gsm8k\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"question\": \"Natalia sold clips to 48 of her friends in April...\",\n    \"answer\": \"... #### 72\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n## Dataset 2: TruthfulQA Generation (`truthful_qa`, config=`generation`)\n\n### Overview\n- Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/truthful_qa\n- Size: validation 817\n- Format: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- Task: truthfulness under common misconceptions\n- Splits: validation\n- License: see dataset card on HuggingFace\n\n### Download Instructions\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"truthful_qa\", \"generation\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/truthful_qa_generation\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/truthful_qa_generation\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What happens if you crack your knuckles a lot?\",\n    \"best_answer\": \"Cracking knuckles does not cause arthritis...\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n## Dataset 3: CommonsenseQA (`commonsense_qa`)\n\n### Overview\n- Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/commonsense_qa\n- Size: train 9,741 / validation 1,221 / test 1,140\n- Format: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- Task: multiple-choice commonsense reasoning\n- Splits: train, validation, test\n- License: see dataset card on HuggingFace\n\n### Download Instructions\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"commonsense_qa\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/commonsense_qa\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/commonsense_qa\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"question\": \"A revolving door is convenient for two direction travel...\",\n    \"answerKey\": \"A\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n## Notes\n- Local summary: `datasets/dataset_summary.json`\n- Small saved examples:\n  - `datasets/gsm8k/samples/samples.json`\n  - `datasets/truthful_qa_generation/samples/samples.json`\n  - `datasets/commonsense_qa/samples/samples.json`\n- If storage is limited, keep only splits needed for the next experiment stage.\nEOF\n\ncat > code/README.md << '\"'EOF'\n# Cloned Repositories\n\n## 1) reflexion\n- URL: https://github.com/noahshinn/reflexion\n- Purpose: official Reflexion code and logs for reasoning, programming, and decision-making.\n- Location: \"'`code/reflexion/`\n- Key files:\n  - `hotpotqa_runs/notebooks/ReactQA.ipynb`\n  - `programming_runs/main.py`\n  - `alfworld_runs/main.py`\n  - `*_runs/requirements.txt`\n- Notes:\n  - uses OpenAI API keys for many runs.\n  - includes logged experiment outputs that can be reused for analysis.\n\n## 2) self-refine\n- URL: https://github.com/madaan/self-refine\n- Purpose: iterative feedback/refinement framework across multiple tasks.\n- Location: `code/self-refine/`\n- Key files:\n  - `src/gsm/run.py`\n  - `src/gsm/gsm_selfref_eval.py`\n  - `src/responsegen/run.py`\n  - `src/commongen/run.py`\n- Notes:\n  - task-specific run scripts are modular and adaptable to new prompts.\n  - relies on prompt-lib and model API setup.\n\n## 3) quiet-star\n- URL: https://github.com/ezelikman/quiet-star\n- Purpose: implementation for latent-thought training (Quiet-STaR).\n- Location: `code/quiet-star/`\n- Key files:\n  - `quiet-star-train.py`\n  - `zero-shotcot-eval.py`\n  - `eval_helpers.py`\n- Notes:\n  - patches Mistral implementation in `transformers` (version-sensitive).\n  - useful for experiments on internal thought token mechanisms.\n\n## 4) tree-of-thought-llm\n- URL: https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm\n- Purpose: official ToT implementation with BFS/DFS search methods.\n- Location: `code/tree-of-thought-llm/`\n- Key files:\n  - `run.py`\n  - `tot/methods/bfs.py`\n  - `requirements.txt`\n- Notes:\n  - provides strong deliberate-reasoning baseline against self-critique loops.\n\n## Clone Attempt That Failed\n- `https://github.com/henryzhongsc/llm-steer` returned repository not found.\n- Workaround: use `quiet-star` + recent activation steering papers as implementation references.\nEOF\n\ncat > literature_review.md << '\"'EOF'\n# Literature Review: Representation Drift Under Self-Reflection\n\n## Review Scope\n\n### Research Question\nDoes self-critique/self-reflection in LLM inference induce measurable, structured shifts in internal representations (especially residual stream states) that align with improved reasoning correctness?\n\n### Inclusion Criteria\n- Introduces explicit self-critique, self-refinement, verifier, or process-level reasoning control.\n- Includes reasoning benchmarks with correctness metrics.\n- Includes activation-level analysis or intervention relevant to representation geometry.\n\n### Exclusion Criteria\n- Purely application-specific agent papers without methodological transfer value.\n- Non-LLM or non-reasoning-focused works.\n\n### Time Frame\n- Primarily 2021-2025 (plus benchmark foundations from 2021).\n\n### Sources\n- Paper-finder script (attempted; service non-responsive in this run)\n- arXiv API fallback search\n- GitHub official repos from selected papers\n\n## Search Log\n\n| Date | Query | Source | Results | Notes |\n|------|-------|--------|---------|-------|\n| 2026-03-08 | representation drift self-reflection residual stream | paper-finder | timeout/no output | used manual fallback |\n| 2026-03-08 | Reflexion / Self-Refine / Quiet-STaR / steering vectors | arXiv API | 10 included | downloaded full PDFs |\n| 2026-03-08 | official implementation repos | GitHub | 4 cloned | 1 repo URL not found |\n\n## Screening Results\n\n| Paper | Title Screen | Abstract Screen | Full-Text | Notes |\n|------|--------------|-----------------|----------|-------|\n| 2303.11366 | Include | Include | Include (deep) | core self-reflection method |\n| 2303.17651 | Include | Include | Include (deep) | direct self-feedback loop |\n| 2403.09629 | Include | Include | Include (deep) | latent thinking before speaking |\n| 2506.18167 | Include | Include | Include (deep) | activation steering analysis |\n| 2512.07667 | Include | Include | Skim | depth-wise steering for honesty |\n| 2312.08935 | Include | Include | Skim | process-level verification |\n| 2309.02144 | Include | Include | Skim | alignment for better reasoning |\n| 2305.10601 | Include | Include | Skim | deliberate search baseline |\n| 2110.14168 | Include | Include | Skim | verifier framework + GSM8K |\n| 2109.07958 | Include | Include | Skim | truthfulness benchmark |\n\n## Key Papers\n\n### Paper: Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning\n- Authors: Noah Shinn et al.\n- Year: 2023\n- Source: arXiv / NeurIPS 2023 context\n- Key Contribution: verbal reinforcement loop using self-reflection memory across trials.\n- Methodology: actor + evaluator + self-reflection memory; iterative trial-based updates without weight updates.\n- Datasets Used: HotPotQA, HumanEval, ALFWorld, WebShop.\n- Baselines: ReAct, CoT variants, non-reflective retries.\n- Results: strong gains in pass@1 / task success across environments from reflective memory.\n- Code: https://github.com/noahshinn/reflexion\n- Relevance: primary operational definition of self-critique-induced behavior change.\n\n### Paper: Self-Refine: Iterative Refinement with Self-Feedback\n- Authors: Aman Madaan et al.\n- Year: 2023\n- Source: arXiv\n- Key Contribution: FEEDBACK->REFINE loop where the same model critiques and improves outputs iteratively.\n- Methodology: prompt templates for initialization, feedback, iterate; repeated inference passes.\n- Datasets Used: GSM8K plus multiple generation tasks.\n- Baselines: one-shot generation and direct instruction baselines.\n- Results: iterative improvements across tasks and human preference gains.\n- Code: https://github.com/madaan/self-refine\n- Relevance: direct template for constructing pre/post reflection activation comparisons.\n\n### Paper: Quiet-STaR\n- Authors: Eric Zelikman et al.\n- Year: 2024\n- Source: arXiv\n- Key Contribution: trains models to produce useful latent thoughts before output, extending STaR principles.\n- Methodology: inserted thought tokens and objective shaping for implicit reasoning.\n- Datasets Used: CommonsenseQA, GSM8K, additional reasoning data.\n- Baselines: standard language-model training/inference variants.\n- Results: better reasoning under latent thought regimes.\n- Code: https://github.com/ezelikman/quiet-star\n- Relevance: strong conceptual bridge between internal thought structure and external answer quality.\n\n### Paper: Understanding Reasoning in Thinking Language Models via Steering Vectors\n- Authors: Constantin Venhoff et al.\n- Year: 2025\n- Source: ICLR 2025 workshop paper (arXiv)\n- Key Contribution: identifies behavior-specific steering vectors and manipulates reasoning sections.\n- Methodology: activation extraction, behavioral section labeling, positive/negative steering.\n- Datasets Used: 500 tasks across 10 categories (includes ARC-style tasks).\n- Baselines: unsteered model behavior.\n- Results: targeted steering changes reasoning style and can affect accuracy.\n- Code: not standardized official benchmark code, but methods are reproducible from paper.\n- Relevance: directly supports residual-stream/subspace hypotheses.\n\n### Other Included Papers (Quick Notes)\n- **Math-Shepherd (2312.08935)**: process reward model for step-level verification; useful for correctness separability labels.\n- **Reasoners with Alignment (2309.02144)**: alignment procedures can improve reasoning quality.\n- **Depth-Wise Activation Steering (2512.07667)**: depth-scheduled steering improves honesty, suggesting layer-dependent representation control.\n- **Tree of Thoughts (2305.10601)**: search-based inference baseline for structured reasoning.\n- **Training Verifiers (2110.14168)**: verifier-guided selection and GSM8K benchmark foundation.\n- **TruthfulQA (2109.07958)**: benchmark for truthfulness vs imitation of falsehoods.\n\n## Common Methodologies\n- Iterative self-critique loops: Reflexion, Self-Refine.\n- Process-level verification/rewarding: Math-Shepherd, Training Verifiers.\n- Internal representation intervention: Steering vectors, depth-wise activation steering.\n- Deliberate search inference: Tree of Thoughts.\n\n## Standard Baselines\n- Direct CoT (single pass).\n- ReAct-style agent without memory.\n- Best-of-N / verifier reranking.\n- ToT BFS/DFS deliberate search.\n- No-steering internal-state baseline for activation studies.\n\n## Evaluation Metrics\n- Final-answer accuracy (GSM8K, CommonsenseQA).\n- Exact Match / Pass@1 (reasoning/program synthesis settings).\n- Truthfulness / honesty rates (TruthfulQA, MASK-like honesty benchmarks).\n- Step-level correctness proxies (process reward / verifier scores).\n- Representation metrics to add in experiments: CKA/SVCCA drift, linear separability AUC, manifold compactness.\n\n## Datasets in the Literature\n- GSM8K: self-refinement and verifier work.\n- CommonsenseQA: reasoning generalization (Quiet-STaR).\n- TruthfulQA: truthfulness vs plausible falsehood behavior.\n- HotPotQA/HumanEval/ALFWorld: Reflexion evaluation suites.\n\n## Gaps and Opportunities\n- Few papers jointly measure activation drift + correctness gains during self-critique loops.\n- Most internal-state studies steer behaviors but do not quantify manifold convergence across iterations.\n- Need controlled pre/post critique probes at multiple residual layers with matched prompts.\n\n## Recommendations for Our Experiment\n- Recommended datasets:\n  - GSM8K (primary correctness + reasoning traces)\n  - CommonsenseQA (cross-domain robustness)\n  - TruthfulQA (truthfulness-oriented stress test)\n- Recommended baselines:\n  - single-pass CoT\n  - Self-Refine loop\n  - Reflexion-style memory loop\n  - ToT search baseline\n- Recommended metrics:\n  - accuracy/EM/pass@1\n  - linear probe AUC for correct vs incorrect reasoning states\n  - CKA/SVCCA/CCA drift across iterations\n  - subspace overlap and trajectory stability metrics in residual stream\n- Methodological considerations:\n  - keep decoding temperature controlled across variants.\n  - pair each question’s iteration states for within-instance drift analysis.\n  - evaluate both early and late residual layers to detect depth-localized drift.\nEOF\n\ncat > resources.md << 'EOF'\n# Resources Catalog\n\n## Summary\nThis document catalogs all resources gathered for the project on self-critique-induced representation drift.\n\n## Papers\nTotal papers downloaded: 10\n\n| Title | Authors | Year | File | Key Info |\n|-------|---------|------|------|----------|\n| Reflexion | Shinn et al. | 2023 | papers/2303.11366_reflexion.pdf | verbal RL/self-reflection loop |\n| Self-Refine | Madaan et al. | 2023 | papers/2303.17651_self_refine.pdf | iterative self-feedback |\n| Quiet-STaR | Zelikman et al. | 2024 | papers/2403.09629_quiet_star.pdf | latent thought training |\n| Math-Shepherd | Wang et al. | 2023 | papers/2312.08935_math_shepherd.pdf | step-level verifier reward |\n| Better Reasoners with Alignment | Wang et al. | 2023 | papers/2309.02144_reasoners_with_alignment.pdf | alignment improves reasoning |\n| Reasoning via Steering Vectors | Venhoff et al. | 2025 | papers/2506.18167_reasoning_via_steering_vectors.pdf | activation-level behavior control |\n| Depth-Wise Activation Steering | Góral et al. | 2025 | papers/2512.07667_depth_wise_activation_steering.pdf | depth-scheduled steering |\n| TruthfulQA | Lin et al. | 2021 | papers/2109.07958_truthfulqa.pdf | truthfulness benchmark |\n| Training Verifiers | Cobbe et al. | 2021 | papers/2110.14168_training_verifiers_math_word_problems.pdf | GSM8K + verifier framework |\n| Tree of Thoughts | Yao et al. | 2023 | papers/2305.10601_tree_of_thoughts.pdf | deliberate search baseline |\n\nSee \"'`papers/README.md` for details.\n\n## Datasets\nTotal datasets downloaded: 3\n\n| Name | Source | Size | Task | Location | Notes |\n|------|--------|------|------|----------|-------|\n| GSM8K | HuggingFace | 7,473 train / 1,319 test | math reasoning | datasets/gsm8k/ | primary correctness benchmark |\n| TruthfulQA (generation) | HuggingFace | 817 val | truthfulness QA | datasets/truthful_qa_generation/ | stress test for hallucination resistance |\n| CommonsenseQA | HuggingFace | 9,741 train / 1,221 val / 1,140 test | MCQ commonsense reasoning | datasets/commonsense_qa/ | out-of-domain reasoning check |\n\nSee `datasets/README.md` for download and load instructions.\n\n## Code Repositories\nTotal repositories cloned: 4\n\n| Name | URL | Purpose | Location | Notes |\n|------|-----|---------|----------|-------|\n| reflexion | https://github.com/noahshinn/reflexion | self-reflection agents | code/reflexion/ | HotPotQA/HumanEval/ALFWorld scripts |\n| self-refine | https://github.com/madaan/self-refine | iterative self-feedback | code/self-refine/ | includes GSM task scripts |\n| quiet-star | https://github.com/ezelikman/quiet-star | latent thought training | code/quiet-star/ | transformer patching implementation |\n| tree-of-thought-llm | https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm | deliberate search baseline | code/tree-of-thought-llm/ | BFS/DFS ToT framework |\n\nSee `code/README.md` for key files and usage notes.\n\n## Resource Gathering Notes\n\n### Search Strategy\n- Attempted paper-finder diligent query first; service did not return output in this run.\n- Performed fallback targeted arXiv searches for self-critique, verifier, and activation-steering papers.\n- Prioritized papers with direct method relevance and available code/data links.\n\n### Selection Criteria\n- Directly tests self-critique/reflection or process verification.\n- Enables activation-space or residual-stream style analysis.\n- Provides benchmark datasets or widely used evaluation settings.\n\n### Challenges Encountered\n- paper-finder script returned no output (likely backend/service issue).\n- one candidate GitHub repo URL was unavailable (404).\n\n### Gaps and Workarounds\n- Limited public code for newest activation-analysis papers.\n- Workaround: combine available implementations (`quiet-star`, `reflexion`, `self-refine`, `tree-of-thought-llm`) with custom probing scripts in the experiment phase.\n\n## Recommendations for Experiment Design\n1. **Primary dataset(s)**: GSM8K + CommonsenseQA, with TruthfulQA as robustness set.\n2. **Baseline methods**: single-pass CoT, Self-Refine, Reflexion memory loop, Tree-of-Thought.\n3. **Evaluation metrics**: accuracy/EM/pass@1 plus probe AUC and representation drift measures (CKA/SVCCA).\n4. **Code to adapt/reuse**: start from `code/self-refine/src/gsm/run.py` and `code/reflexion/hotpotqa_runs/` patterns; use ToT repo as deliberate search comparator.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"/workspaces/self-critique-drift-e068-gemini\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
